      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int (\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{5}{1-{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x$  for $|x|<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{5}{1-{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
